    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d730">

                <pb facs="0991" n="889" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg889"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Italy/211</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-10">March 10, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Italian Ambassador asked me to bear in mind that he stood ready to take up
                    the question of debt negotiations whenever this Government was inclined to do
                    so. He understood that the debt situation vis-à-vis Great Britain was far more
                    important than that vis-à-vis Italy and that he was merely biding his time until
                    the proper moment. Inasmuch as he was not going to press for any debt
                    negotiations, he did not wish to convey the impression that he was indifferent
                    to the subject. He asked me to give him a tip whenever the right moment had
                    arrived for him to open up the subject.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
